[Cheonji Ilbo, Yeosu = Reporter Lee Bong-hwa] Ahead of the 2026 Yeosu World Island Expo, Yeosu City is re-examining the value of its representative inhabited island, Sonjukdo.

Sonjukdo is a patriotic island where General Lee Dae-won died in battle during the Imjin War, commemorated by a statue of the general and the Chungnyeolsa Shrine.

Throughout the island village, residents have created unique gardens and murals, earning it the nickname &ldquo;Garden on the Sea.&rdquo;

Mountains such as Gitdaebong and Samgaksan, along with coastal trails, offer trekking routes where visitors can enjoy the breathtaking scenery of the Dadohae.

Traditional customs like Hwajeon-nori and pure Korean place names reflect the island&rsquo;s unique identity and everyday culture.

Rich fishing grounds have sustained Sonjukdo for generations, fostering community traditions such as Gilgut-nori, a ritual tied to the sea.

Blending history, nature, and culture, Sonjukdo has established itself not just as an &ldquo;Island to Visit&rdquo; but as an &ldquo;Island to Return To.&rdquo;
